@@ -175,3 +175,19 @@ Project agents override user agents with the same name when `agentScope: "both"`
 - Parallel model-visible output is capped at 50 KB per task; full results remain in tool details
 - Agents discovered fresh on each invocation (allows editing mid-session)
 - Parallel mode limited to 8 tasks, 4 concurrent
+
+## Live team collaboration
+
+For a parallel dispatch, set `collaboration: true` and give every task a unique
+`id`, for example `{ collaboration: true, tasks: [{id: "research", agent:
+"worker", task: "Investigate"}, {id: "implement", agent: "worker", task: "Implement"}] }`.
+Workers use `crew_roster({})` to discover instance IDs, then
+`crew_send({to: "implement", body: "The endpoint requires cursor pagination"})`
+or `crew_send({broadcast: true, body: "The endpoint requires cursor pagination"})`.
+Incoming findings enter model context at the next turn boundary automatically.
+Sending reports accepted and failed recipients; it does not await a response.
+IDs are scoped to one dispatch. Pending and finished workers cannot receive new
+messages. Cancellation cleans up the team's temporary mailboxes after children stop.
+This implementation uses local temporary storage and does not recover from host crashes.
+
+This interface returns `{me, peers: [{address}]}` for the roster (other teammates only), and `{delivered, rejected}` for sends. Findings use the `body` field and a documented limit of 65536 UTF-8 bytes.
